
This illustrates a pmf calculation for a reaction. A QM/MM
calculation is performed with complete solute flexibility.
The reaction is the Michael addition of methane thiolate to
methyl crotonate. The reaction coordinate is taken as the
Cbeta - S distance. The solute energetics are evaluated with
AM1; the solute-solvent interactions use the unscaled CM1A
charges and generic L-J parameters for the solute atoms. The 
solvent box contains 390 OPLS-UA methanol molecules.

Only one window is executed; however, the entire pmf could be
run by chaining jobs or as separate jobs on multiple processors.
See the dihpmf/fullpmf directory for more information.

Four equilibration runs of 250K each and four averaging runs of
250K each are executed. For the real calculation, 2M configurations
of equilibration and 4M of averaging would be reasonable.

Time required for the 2M configurations: 2.2 h on an R5000 SGI.
(This includes the execution of 30,000 AM1 calculations.)

Use bossinfo and ChemEdit to graphically display the results:
bossinfo < r1850ote2 > out
ce -i mol out
